      "id": "broad-array-communications-antenna-st-croix-u-s-virgin-islands-20260626195955",
      "category": "governemt",
      "title": "Broad Array Communications Antenna – St. Croix, U.S. Virgin Islands",
      "description": "This project required far more than the application of protective coatings. I was responsible for mobilizing the project from Northeast Ohio to St. Croix, coordinating every phase of transportation and jobsite logistics before work could even begin.  A dedicated shipping container was loaded in Akron, Ohio, transported by rail to Miami, Florida, and then shipped by sea to St. Croix. Every tool, piece of equipment, coating, consumable, and safety supply had to be carefully planned and accounted for before departure. Unlike a typical domestic project, replacing forgotten materials wasn’t as simple as visiting a local supplier—it could delay the project for weeks while replacement items were shipped to the island.  Once on site, the work involved protective coating application on a massive communications antenna, requiring detailed planning, specialized access equipment, and disciplined execution. The successful completion of the project reflected not only technical coating expertise, but also the ability to manage complex logistics, transportation, and field operations from start to finish.",
